<H1>WmiChannels memory&nbsp;leak </H1></DIV>
<DIV class=3D"date-comments">
<P class=3D"fl"><EM>Posted on November 18, 2010</EM> 			    				    					=
    by=20
<EM><A title=3D"Posts by Ariela Boursi" =
href=3D"http://wcfpro.wordpress.com/author/arielasivan/"=20
rel=3D"author">Ariela Boursi</A></EM></P>
<P class=3D"fr"><SPAN class=3D"comments"><A =
href=3D"http://wcfpro.wordpress.com/2010/11/18/wmichannels-memory-leak/#c=
omments">0</A></SPAN></P></DIV>
<DIV class=3D"clear"></DIV><BR>
<DIV class=3D"entry">
<P>The following bug happens in a very specific scenario in which one =
element is=20
both the server side for one WCF operation, and the client side for=20
another&nbsp; WCF operation, and all services work in a singleton mode =
(the=20
InstanceContextMode is single). Since we encounter this scenario, and =
spent=20
hours trying to analyze it, we thought we might not be the only ones, =
and this=20
post can be useful for others =E2=80=A6</P>
<H2>Symptom</H2>
<P>This bug happens only in .Net 3.5 when there is a load from the =
following=20
scenario:</P>
<OL>
  <LI>=E2=80=9CA=E2=80=9D starts a WCF operation very often
  <LI>=E2=80=9CB=E2=80=9D is also the server side for the operation that =
started from =E2=80=9CA=E2=80=9D and=20
  also the client side for the operation to =E2=80=9CC=E2=80=9D.
  <LI>The channel from =E2=80=9CB=E2=80=9D to =E2=80=9CC=E2=80=9D often =
get faulted (for example =E2=80=9CC=E2=80=9D is=20
  sometimes down), and =E2=80=9CB=E2=80=9D calls Abort() on the channel, =
and creates in this=20
  case a new one. </LI></OL>
<P><A href=3D"http://wcfpro.files.wordpress.com/2010/11/flow2.png"><IMG =
style=3D"border-width: 0px; padding-top: 0px; padding-right: 0px; =
padding-left: 0px; display: inline; background-image: none;"=20
title=3D"FLOW" border=3D"0" alt=3D"FLOW" =
src=3D"http://wcfpro.files.wordpress.com/2010/11/flow_thumb2.png?w=3D240&=
amp;h=3D82"=20
width=3D"240" height=3D"82"></A></P>
<P>After a while, you will noticea huge memory&nbsp; consumption of =
WmiChannels=20
(System.ServiceModel.Channels.IChannel) from the InstanceContext =
object.</P>
<P>
<DIV style=3D"margin: 0px; padding: 0px; float: none; display: inline;" =
id=3D"scid:57F11A72-B0E5-49c7-9094-E3A15BD5B5E6:5df71505-ec86-40e9-a5be-0=
36319cf837f"=20
class=3D"wlWriterEditableSmartContent"><PRE style=3D"overflow: auto; =
background-color: rgb(239, 239, 239);"><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, =
