<P></P>
<P>The reason this memory leak happens is that when calling =
CreateChannel(Type,=20
EndpointAddress, Uri ), the following lines are executed:</P>
<P>
<DIV style=3D"margin: 0px; padding: 0px; float: none; display: inline;" =
id=3D"scid:57F11A72-B0E5-49c7-9094-E3A15BD5B5E6:dd667bc9-03a6-4037-b9b1-f=
3ba82336852"=20
class=3D"wlWriterEditableSmartContent"><PRE style=3D"overflow: auto; =
background-color: rgb(239, 239, 239);"><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, =
0);"> </SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">if</SPAN><SPAN =
style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> ((current </SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: =
rgb(0, 0, 0);">!=3D</SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> =
</SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">null</SPAN><SPAN =
style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);">) </SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, =
0);">&amp;&amp;</SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> =
(current.InstanceContext </SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, =
0);">!=3D</SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> </SPAN><SPAN =
style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 255);">null</SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, =
0, 0);">))=0A=
 {=0A=
     =
current.InstanceContext.WmiChannels.Add((IChannel)serviceChannel.Proxy);=0A=
     serviceChannel.WmiInstanceContext </SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: =
rgb(0, 0, 0);">=3D</SPAN><SPAN style=3D"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"> =
current.InstanceContext;=0A=
 }=0A=
</SPAN></PRE>
<P><!-- Code inserted with Steve Dunn's Windows Live Writer Code =
Formatter Plugin.  http://dunnhq.com --></P></DIV>
<P>WmiChannel is created, and added on the InstanceContext object. The =
problem=20
is that Remove from WmiChannels collection =
(WmiChannels.Remove((IChannel)) is=20
called only in =E2=80=9COnClose()=E2=80=9D and not in =
=E2=80=9ConAbort()=E2=80=9D. </P>
<P>Since this is a singleton mode, and it=E2=80=99s the same =
InstanceContext object for=20
all requests,</P>
<P>the list of wmichannels is getting larger all the time, and its never =

cleaned.</P>
<H2>Solution</H2>
<P>This problem is solved in .Net 4.0.</P>
<P>There are several workarounds for the problem in .Net 3.5:</P>
<P>One solution is to change the InstanceMode of the services from =
singleton to=20
PerCall. If this is not possible, the call from =E2=80=9CB=E2=80=9D to =
=E2=80=9CC=E2=80=9D will have to be=20
executed on a different thread.</P>
